   "source": [
    "# Case Study 01 — Credit Scoring: Logistic Regression & Scorecard\n",
    "\n",
    "**Erick Condoy** · Economist (UNL) · Quant Researcher  \n",
    "Repository: [credit-risk-lab](https://github.com/EryckFCS/credit-risk-lab)\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "Build a **production-grade credit scorecard** following the industry-standard methodology:\n",
    "Logistic Regression on WoE features → Probability of Default (PD) → Scorecard scaling (PDO method).\n",
    "\n",
    "| Section | Content |\n",
    "|---------|---------|\n",
    "| 1 | Load Artefacts from Notebook 02 |\n",
    "| 2 | Logistic Regression — Baseline Model |\n",
    "| 3 | Model Validation: KS / Gini / AUC / CAP |\n",
    "| 4 | Calibration Check |\n",
    "| 5 | Scorecard Scaling (PDO Method) |\n",
    "| 6 | Score Distribution & Cut-off Analysis |\n",
    "| 7 | Population Stability Index (PSI) |\n",
    "| 8 | Model Card & Export |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Theoretical Framework\n",
    "\n",
    "**Logistic Regression on WoE features:**\n",
    "$$\\log\\left(\\frac{p}{1-p}\\right) = \\beta_0 + \\sum_{j=1}^{n} \\beta_j \\cdot \\text{WoE}_{ij}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Scorecard scaling (PDO — Points to Double the Odds):**\n",
    "$$\\text{Score} = \\text{Offset} + \\text{Factor} \\times \\ln(\\text{Odds})$$\n",
    "where $\\text{Factor} = \\frac{\\text{PDO}}{\\ln(2)}$ and $\\text{Offset} = \\text{Base Score} - \\text{Factor} \\times \\ln(\\text{Base Odds})$\n",
    "\n",
    "Standard parameters: Base Score = 600, Base Odds = 50:1, PDO = 20 (Siddiqi, 2006)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "import sys, warnings, json\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.ticker as mticker\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.calibration import calibration_curve, CalibratedClassifierCV\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (roc_auc_score, roc_curve, brier_score_loss,\n",
    "                              classification_report, confusion_matrix)\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "import pickle\n",
    "\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.float_format', '{:.4f}'.format)\n",
    "\n",
    "REPO_ROOT = Path().resolve().parents[1]\n",
    "ARTEFACTS = Path('../artefacts')\n",
    "REPORTS   = Path('../reports')\n",
    "REPORTS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\n",
    "    'figure.facecolor':'white','axes.facecolor':'white',\n",
    "    'axes.spines.top':False,'axes.spines.right':False,\n",
    "    'axes.edgecolor':'#dcd9d5','axes.labelcolor':'#28251d',\n",
    "    'xtick.color':'#7a7974','ytick.color':'#7a7974',\n",
    "    'font.family':'sans-serif','font.size':10,\n",
    "    'axes.titlesize':11,'axes.titleweight':'semibold','figure.dpi':120,\n",
    "})\n",
    "TEAL='#01696f'; MAROON='#a12c7b'; GRAY='#bab9b4'; GREEN='#437a22'; ORANGE='#964219'\n",
    "print(f'Python {sys.version}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 1. Load Artefacts from Notebook 02"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train = pd.read_parquet(ARTEFACTS / 'X_train_woe.parquet')\n",
    "X_test  = pd.read_parquet(ARTEFACTS / 'X_test_woe.parquet')\n",
    "y_train = pd.read_parquet(ARTEFACTS / 'y_train.parquet').squeeze()\n",
    "y_test  = pd.read_parquet(ARTEFACTS / 'y_test.parquet').squeeze()\n",
    "iv_df   = pd.read_csv(ARTEFACTS / 'iv_table.csv', index_col=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(ARTEFACTS / 'selected_features.json') as f:\n",
    "    feat_meta = json.load(f)\n",
    "FINAL_FEATURES = feat_meta['woe_features']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Train: {X_train.shape}  |  Test: {X_test.shape}')\n",
    "print(f'Train DR: {y_train.mean():.2%}  |  Test DR: {y_test.mean():.2%}')\n",
    "print(f'WoE features: {FINAL_FEATURES[:5]} ...')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 2. Logistic Regression — Baseline Model"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# WoE features are already on a comparable scale; StandardScaler ensures\n",
    "# numerical stability for the solver but doesn't change the model structure.\n",
    "model = Pipeline([\n",
    "    ('scaler', StandardScaler()),\n",
    "    ('lr', LogisticRegression(\n",
    "        C=1.0,                    # L2 regularisation — tune in notebook 04\n",
    "        class_weight='balanced',  # handles 22% imbalance\n",
    "        solver='lbfgs',\n",
    "        max_iter=1000,\n",
    "        random_state=42,\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "model.fit(X_train[FINAL_FEATURES], y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "y_prob_train = model.predict_proba(X_train[FINAL_FEATURES])[:, 1]\n",
    "y_prob_test  = model.predict_proba(X_test[FINAL_FEATURES])[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "lr = model.named_steps['lr']\n",
    "coef_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'feature': FINAL_FEATURES,\n",
    "    'coefficient': lr.coef_[0]\n",
    "}).sort_values('coefficient', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Model fitted. Coefficients:')\n",
    "display(coef_df.style.bar(subset=['coefficient'],\n",
    "        color=[MAROON, TEAL], align='zero').format({'coefficient':'{:.4f}'}))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 3. Model Validation: KS / Gini / AUC / CAP"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def ks_statistic(y_true, y_prob):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic: max separation between Good and Bad CDFs.\"\"\"\n",
    "    df_ = pd.DataFrame({'prob': y_prob, 'target': y_true}).sort_values('prob')\n",
    "    total_bad  = (y_true == 1).sum()\n",
    "    total_good = (y_true == 0).sum()\n",
    "    df_['cum_bad']  = (df_['target'] == 1).cumsum() / total_bad\n",
    "    df_['cum_good'] = (df_['target'] == 0).cumsum() / total_good\n",
    "    ks = (df_['cum_bad'] - df_['cum_good']).abs().max()\n",
    "    ks_thresh = df_.loc[(df_['cum_bad'] - df_['cum_good']).abs().idxmax(), 'prob']\n",
    "    return ks, ks_thresh, df_\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def gini_coefficient(y_true, y_prob):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Gini = 2*AUC - 1.\"\"\"\n",
    "    auc = roc_auc_score(y_true, y_prob)\n",
    "    return 2 * auc - 1, auc\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def cap_ratio(y_true, y_prob):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Accuracy Ratio from CAP curve (= Gini).\"\"\"\n",
    "    df_ = pd.DataFrame({'prob': y_prob, 'target': y_true}).sort_values('prob', ascending=False)\n",
    "    n   = len(df_)\n",
    "    n_b = y_true.sum()\n",
    "    df_['cum_pct_pop'] = np.arange(1, n+1) / n\n",
    "    df_['cum_pct_bad'] = df_['target'].cumsum() / n_b\n",
    "    # Area under model curve (trapezoidal)\n",
    "    auc_model  = np.trapz(df_['cum_pct_bad'], df_['cum_pct_pop'])\n",
    "    auc_random = 0.5\n",
    "    auc_perf   = 1 - (y_true.mean() / 2)\n",
    "    ar = (auc_model - auc_random) / (auc_perf - auc_random)\n",
    "    return ar, df_\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- Compute metrics ----\n",
    "ks_tr, _, _    = ks_statistic(y_train, y_prob_train)\n",
    "ks_te, ks_thr, ks_df = ks_statistic(y_test, y_prob_test)\n",
    "gini_tr, auc_tr = gini_coefficient(y_train, y_prob_train)\n",
    "gini_te, auc_te = gini_coefficient(y_test,  y_prob_test)\n",
    "ar_tr, _       = cap_ratio(y_train, y_prob_train)\n",
    "ar_te, cap_df  = cap_ratio(y_test,  y_prob_test)\n",
    "brier_te       = brier_score_loss(y_test, y_prob_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "metrics = {\n",
    "    'KS':     {'train': ks_tr,   'test': ks_te,   'threshold_good': 0.30, 'threshold_min': 0.20},\n",
    "    'Gini':   {'train': gini_tr, 'test': gini_te, 'threshold_good': 0.40, 'threshold_min': 0.30},\n",
    "    'AUC':    {'train': auc_tr,  'test': auc_te,  'threshold_good': 0.70, 'threshold_min': 0.65},\n",
    "    'AR/CAP': {'train': ar_tr,   'test': ar_te,   'threshold_good': 0.40, 'threshold_min': 0.30},\n",
    "    'Brier':  {'train': None,    'test': brier_te,'threshold_good': 0.15, 'threshold_min': 0.20},  # lower=better\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print('╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗')\n",
    "print('║            MODEL VALIDATION REPORT                         ║')\n",
    "print('╠══════════╦══════════╦══════════╦═══════════╦═══════════════╣')\n",
    "print('║ Metric   ║  Train   ║  Test    ║ Threshold ║ Status        ║')\n",
    "print('╠══════════╬══════════╬══════════╬═══════════╬═══════════════╣')\n",
    "for name, vals in metrics.items():\n",
    "    tr_s = f\"{vals['train']:.4f}\" if vals['train'] is not None else '  —   '\n",
    "    te_v = vals['test']\n",
    "    thr  = vals['threshold_good']\n",
    "    # For Brier: lower is better\n",
    "    ok = te_v <= thr if name == 'Brier' else te_v >= thr\n",
    "    status = '✅ PASS' if ok else '⚠️  CHECK'\n",
    "    print(f\"║ {name:<8} ║ {tr_s:<8} ║ {te_v:.4f}   ║ {thr:.2f}      ║ {status:<13} ║\")\n",
    "print('╚══════════╩══════════╩══════════╩═══════════╩═══════════════╝')\n",
    "print(f'\\nKS threshold score: {ks_thr:.4f}  (optimal cut-off for KS maximisation)')"
   ]
  },
